b3chat channel plugin for Claude Code

This folder is derived from the official Telegram channel plugin for Claude Code:
  - Source: anthropics/claude-plugins-official, external_plugins/telegram
  - Version: 0.0.7 (Claude Code plugin cache: claude-plugins-official/telegram/0.0.7)
  - License: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this folder, copied unchanged)
  - Copyright: Anthropic, PBC and the original contributors

Files copied: server.ts, package.json, bun.lock, LICENSE.
The copied server.ts came from the local plugin cache, which differs from the
marketplace copy of 0.0.7 by one local patch (reply_to_message_id / reply_to_user /
reply_to_text in inbound meta). That patch is kept.

Changes made by the b3rys team (b3os) — every changed spot is also listed in the
header comment of server.ts:
  1. State directory from the required env B3CHAT_STATE_DIR (no Telegram default).
  2. Bot token from B3CHAT_BOT_TOKEN and API base from B3CHAT_API_BASE in STATE_DIR/.env;
     the API base must be https:// or http://127.0.0.1 / http://localhost.
  3. Access mode defaults to static (B3CHAT_ACCESS_MODE), no pairing.
  4. grammy Bot uses apiRoot = B3CHAT_API_BASE.
  5. New access.json field ownerChat; permission requests go only there and explain
     the text reply "yes <code>" / "no <code>".
  6. DM permission is decided by chat.id in allowFrom (b3chat private room id differs
     from the sender id).
  7. File attachments are not supported yet: reply with files and download_attachment
     return an error; inbound photos deliver their caption only.
  8. MCP server name "b3chat" and b3chat wording in the instructions.
Added files: b3chat.ts (helpers), tests, README.md, NOTICE.
Plugin layout copied from the original: .claude-plugin/plugin.json (name b3chat),
.mcp.json (same command pattern, server name b3chat), .npmrc (unchanged).
package.json: name "b3chat-channel", start script uses --frozen-lockfile, test script.
